{
  "id": "25361_chinmokusuru",
  "headword": "{沈黙|ちんもく}する",
  "reading": "ちんもくする",
  "romaji": "chinmokusuru",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "to remain silent; to fall silent",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to remain silent; to fall silent; to say nothing",
      "explanation": "To deliberately keep quiet or stop speaking, often implying a meaningful or tense silence."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "25361_chinmokusuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}は{沈黙|ちんもく}を{守|まも}った。",
      "english": "He maintained his silence.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "25361_chinmokusuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "その{質問|しつもん}に{対|たい}して、{全員|ぜんいん}が{沈黙|ちんもく}した。",
      "english": "Everyone fell silent at that question.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "25361_chinmokusuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{沈黙|ちんもく}は{金|きん}なり。",
      "english": "Silence is golden. (proverb)",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "25361_chinmokusuru_ex4",
      "japanese": "{不正|ふせい}を{見|み}ても{沈黙|ちんもく}することは、{加担|かたん}しているのと{同|おな}じだ。",
      "english": "Remaining silent even when you see wrongdoing is the same as being complicit.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Implies a deliberate, often weighted silence — not simply being quiet. The noun {沈黙|ちんもく} is used even more frequently than the verb form. Often carries dramatic or serious overtones.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {沈黙|ちんもく}を{守|まも}る: to maintain silence\n- {沈黙|ちんもく}を{破|やぶ}る: to break the silence\n- {沈黙|ちんもく}が{流|なが}れる: silence falls (over a room)\n- {長|なが}い{沈黙|ちんもく}: a long silence\n- {重|おも}い{沈黙|ちんもく}: a heavy silence\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {黙|だま}る: to become silent — more colloquial and everyday\n- {無言|むごん}: wordlessness — describes the state of not speaking rather than the act\n- {黙秘|もくひ}する: to remain silent (legal) — specifically exercising the right to silence",
